# GroomPace — Project Rules

## What this is
A groom-speed tracker PWA ("Strava for groomers") with one real production
user (the developer's wife, a professional groomer). Production = main branch,
auto-deployed by Vercel to groom-pace.vercel.app. Production must never break.

## Architecture (current)
- Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS. No framework, no build step, no bundler. Keep it that way
  unless explicitly told otherwise.
- index.html currently contains everything (~3500 lines). Splitting into
  index.html + app.js + style.css is approved. Introducing React/Vue/Vite is NOT
  approved without explicit permission.
- sw.js = service worker (network-first for index.html, cache-first otherwise).
- manifest.json = PWA manifest.

## Sacred invariants — breaking these loses real user data
1. localStorage key 'groompace-v5' and SCHEMA_VERSION/MIGRATIONS logic must
   keep loading existing data. Never rename keys without a copy-over migration.
2. IndexedDB 'groompace-photos' stores photos as 'idb:...' refs. Never change
   DB_NAME or the ref format without a migration.
3. Every release MUST bump CACHE_NAME in sw.js, or returning users get stuck
   on stale versions.
4. Export/Import (backup/restore) must keep working in every change.

## Code patterns to preserve
- Event delegation: all interactivity uses data-action attributes dispatched
  through the ACTIONS map and wireActions(). Never add inline onclick handlers
  except event.stopPropagation() on lightbox images.
- R() re-renders everything; form input values are snapshotted/restored across
  renders (file inputs excluded — browsers forbid setting their value).
- All user-provided strings go through esc() before rendering.
- Single quiet helper style: short names (S, R, vib, esc) are intentional.

## Design system
- Colors/typography via CSS custom properties in :root (warm cream palette,
  rose primary #D4849A/#B8667E, Fraunces serif headings, DM Sans body).
  Dark mode via prefers-color-scheme. All new UI must use the existing
  CSS variables, not hardcoded colors.
- Mobile-first, max-width 430px, bottom tab navigation, safe-area insets.

## Workflow rules (non-negotiable)
- Work in small slices. After each completed slice: STOP, summarize what
  changed and why, and ask the developer to test before continuing.
- Suggest a git commit message after each working slice. Never auto-commit.
- Explain reasoning as you go — the developer is a CS student learning from
  this process. Brief "why" notes beat silent changes.
- Never modify the MIGRATIONS, load(), save(), or photo IDB functions without
  flagging it loudly first.
- If a task is ambiguous, ask one clarifying question instead of guessing.

## Out of scope until explicitly approved
Backend, accounts, login, cloud sync, online leaderboards, frameworks,
build tooling, TypeScript migration.
